Vendored servo models
=====================

Only files whose licence allows redistribution live here. servos/cad.py looks
here first, and uses a file only if its sha256 matches the pin in
servos/catalog.py. Models without a stated licence (ROBOTIS, Waveshare) are
not vendored: they are downloaded into the cache on first use instead.

STS3215_03a.step
----------------
Feetech STS3215 servo, simplified solid model (horns fused into the case).

  Source:   TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100, STEP/SO100/STS3215_03a.step
            https://github.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100
            commit 5f6d2b876a53a4872e405b991dd925556c9e38a4
  URL:      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100/5f6d2b876a53a4872e405b991dd925556c9e38a4/STEP/SO100/STS3215_03a.step
  sha256:   cacd717c2f22bec856fdace2c3bc9fa58084d54b6e70378eae90562f34df93ef
  Licence:  Apache License 2.0 (the SO-ARM100 repository's LICENSE, copied
            unchanged as LICENSE-SO-ARM100 next to this file). The upstream
            repository has no NOTICE file.
  Changes:  none. The file is byte-for-byte the upstream file. spiderpig
            transforms it into its servo frame and cuts the fused output horn
            away at load time (servos/catalog.py, servos/model.py); nothing is
            written back.
